    {
      "id": "fda22780b4d0",
      "kind": "character",
      "chamber": 2,
      "seed": 2754979521,
      "data": {
        "lines": [
          "Shh. Aisle seat's yours. It's warm, I know. They all are.",
          "Tobiah's still down there giving the A. He's been giving it since I started this job.",
          "I used to work the neon over in The Lush. Everything there was ON. Here nothing is ON. Here everything is nearly.",
          "See the gold under the curtain? One inch. It has been one inch for as long as I've been counting.",
          "Lumen asked me once what's behind it. I said: the same room, a second later. She hasn't come back.",
          "Sit. Don't wait for it. Waiting is the show."
        ],
        "look": {
          "accent": "#ffb347",
          "coat": "#1a2a4a",
          "hat": "cap"
        },
        "name": "Ves, the night attendant"
      },
      "by": "command:claude",
      "at": 1792015073519
    },
    {
      "id": "1e4badd43fe0",
      "kind": "note",
      "chamber": 2,
      "seed": 2661694069,
      "data": {
        "text": "Architect, you asked what I would put behind the curtain if you let me build it. Nothing. I beg you, nothing. The moment there is a stage there will be a first act, and the moment there is a first act someone will cough and someone will check the time and the seats will go cold one by one. Leave the inch. Leave the gold line under the hem. I have sat in the fourth row for what feels like years, and I have never once wanted it to start. Odile says she tried to map this house and the page kept coming back blank except for the words NOT YET. Keep it that way. — V.",
        "title": "Letters to the Architect, page 10"
      },
      "by": "command:claude",
      "at": 1792015073519
    },
    {
      "id": "b54c6f9ffea5",
      "kind": "cat",
      "chamber": 2,
      "seed": 3484196856,
      "data": {
        "name": "Intermission",
        "says": "The cat sits exactly on the gold line under the curtain, half in the light, half in the dark, and will not be moved. It is the only one here who has already decided to stay."
      },
      "by": "command:claude",
      "at": 1792015073519
    }
